Symbiont - AI Agent Runtime and DSL

Usage: symbi [COMMAND]

Commands:
  init         Create a new Symbiont project (symbiont.toml, agents/, policies/, docker-compose.yml, .env)
  up           Start the Symbiont runtime with auto-configuration
  doctor       Check system health and dependencies
  audit        Inspect protected run evidence
  invocation   Inspect and reconcile retained invocation outcomes
  improvement  Opt in, evaluate and release governed workflow instructions
  logs         Show runtime logs
  status       Show running agents, routes, and I/O handlers
  new          Create a new project from a template
  run          Run a single agent and exit
  tools        Manage ToolClad tool manifests
  mcp          Start MCP server (stdio transport) for AI assistant integration
  agents-md    Generate AGENTS.md from agent DSL definitions
  dsl          Parse and execute DSL
  fmt          Canonical-format Symbi (.symbi) source files
  chat         Manage chat channel adapters (Slack, Teams, Mattermost)
  skills       Manage agent skills (load, verify, sign, scan)
  cron         Manage cron-scheduled agent jobs
  shell        Interactive agent orchestration shell
  repl         Interactive DSL REPL (forwards to the repl-cli binary)
  schemapin    TOFU integrity pinning for MCP server configs (used by SessionStart hooks)
  policy       Evaluate Cedar authorization policies against tool-call inputs
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
